From afb1bd1e497d7cb4e96151975188b29057cb45db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Bollerup <mail@r2x2.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:49:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] gemma4: K-only KV for k_eq_v full layers and GeGLU split
 on prefill

- NINFERNO_GEMMA4_SHARED_VALUES=1|2: the full layers keep FP8 K and only V's
  rotated dimensions (1), or nothing of V, its rotated pairs turned back from
  K by RoPE inside the attention kernel (2). 262K context fits a 24 GB card.
- NINFERNO_GEMMA4_GEGLU_SPLIT_MIN_T=N: calls of N+ columns project gate/up
  through the tuned linear route and apply GeGLU after it; the fused GeGLU
  epilogue ran the generic W4A4 kernel (31B QAT-NVFP4 prefill 2.5K -> 4.1K tok/s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
